      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "P06 rescope: spec internalization + dogfood instead of plan §4 'Hardening + GA'",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D02": {
      "alternatives": [
        "python-callable-only (every check needs a code change)",
        "hybrid (yaml + python escape hatch)",
        "defer to v0.2.1"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T19:48:55.001291Z",
      "id": "D02",
      "rationale": "Bottleneck is non-coders authoring audits, not expressing arbitrary logic. YAML + registry of built-in kinds (file_exists, regex_match, json_path_value, pytest_pass, coverage_min, numeric_threshold, command_exit_zero) lets check-authors stay in YAML; new kinds are a code change. Hybrid escape hatch can come later if real example pushes against the registry.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "B019 audit-check DSL: yaml declarative + check-kind registry",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D03": {
      "alternatives": [
        "audit link required at hypothesis open time",
        "audit link fully optional"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T19:49:01.231132Z",
      "id": "D03",
      "rationale": "Audit link gates the commitment, not the exploration. Forcing audit at hypothesis open time forces premature audit design; making it fully optional fails the verify-before-claim rule. Permissive open + required audit on set-verdict matches the dogfood workflow.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "B020 hypothesis lifecycle: audit-link required at set-verdict only",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D04": {
      "alternatives": [
        "mandatory everywhere (files + URLs)",
        "fully optional",
        "defer to v0.2.1"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T19:49:06.729261Z",
      "id": "D04",
      "rationale": "Local file integrity is cheap to enforce; URL integrity is a different problem (provenance + fetch policy). Mandatory-everywhere couples the registry to network state at registration. eawf artifact verify recomputes on demand for both cases.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "B021 artifact registry: sha256 mandatory for files, optional for URLs",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D05": {
      "alternatives": [
        "run on every state mutation",
        "manual-only (no auto trigger)",
        "defer to v0.2.1"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T19:49:13.099461Z",
      "id": "D05",
      "rationale": "Phase close is the natural integrity boundary; manual run is the escape hatch for debugging. Every-mutation is too slow on hot paths like wave dispatch; manual-only is easy to forget. Failures block phase close; --force requires audit reason so the bypass is recorded.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "B022 integrity runner: auto on phase close + opt-in eawf validate --integrity",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D06": {
      "alternatives": [
        "hand-edit state.json now",
        "ship the verbs as a P06 follow-up commit before tagging v0.1.0"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T19:49:20.589570Z",
      "id": "D06",
      "rationale": "v0.1 CLI lacks 'eawf audit set-verdict' and 'eawf backlog set-priority' verbs. Hand-editing state.json would violate AGENTS.md rule 4 (state CLI is the only mutator). Safer to ship the verbs in P07 and do the retro-stamping (A01..A06 verdicts; B015/B017 P2->P1) at P07 closeout in one pass.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "Defer retro audit-verdict + backlog priority-bumps to P07 CLI completeness",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D07": {
      "alternatives": [
        "squash-merge (collapses history; rejected — incident 2026-05-10 PR #3 squashed by ship skill, reverted via force-push, redone as rebase-merge in PR #4)",
        "merge-commit (disabled at repo level)"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T20:35:25.648863Z",
      "id": "D07",
      "rationale": "Squash collapses per-wave/per-commit history into a single fat commit on main, losing the symbol-prefixed audit trail (e.g. [P06-W05] [P06-CORE]) that AGENTS.md commit-prefix rule and the wave/audit chain depend on for reconstructibility from git log. Rebase-merge preserves linear, individual commits with their original messages — matches the cherry-pick discipline that already feeds the long-running phase branch. Merge-commits forbidden by repo settings (mergeCommitAllowed=false). Default for all phase PRs unless explicitly overridden.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "PR merge strategy: rebase-and-merge; never squash, never merge-commit",
      "superseded_by": null
    },
    "D08": {
      "alternatives": [
        "Adopt review-driven PR cadence immediately (rejected: mid-game policy churn)",
        "Lock per-phase PR forever (rejected: pre-decides v0.2.0 retro)"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-05-10T21:26:53.450950Z",
      "id": "D08",
      "rationale": "User proposed shifting from per-phase PR to review-driven + version-bump PR mid-v0.2. Mid-stream workflow change = state-of-record drift risk; defer re-evaluation to v0.2.0 cut, when iter/phase aggregation pattern is fully exercised.",
      "scope_id": "EAWF",
      "status": "active",
      "summary": "Defer PR-cadence policy change until v0.2.0 ship",
      "superseded_by": null
    }
  },
